      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T07:14:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before this refactor, sensors[sensorName] was reset to nullptr regardless of hwmonFile validity. Now the early return on !hwmonFile skips that reset, so a stale sensor can persist on the temp1 path when hwmonFile is invalid. Is this intentional?",
      "revId": "9d0109198b605d0aabc1662e1fbc131d63badbb8",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96140df1_eec88858",
        "filename": "src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003102
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T08:17:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was not intentional,the fix clears the stale sensor entry on invalid hwmonFile so behavior stays consistent with the pre-refactor logic.\n\nadded a reset of sensors[sensorName] to nullptr before returning on invalid hwmonFile, so stale sensor state is not preserved.",
      "parentUuid": "1aa57b89_3bb834bb",
      "revId": "9d0109198b605d0aabc1662e1fbc131d63badbb8",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
